ecord holder, although she set that in the high-tech suit era; American " [:a {:href "/athletes/126679"} "Missy Franklin"] ", gold medalist at the 2013 Worlds; and Australians " [:a {:href "/athletes/129061"} "Emma McKeon"] ", ranked #3 in the world in 2016, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/115711"} "Bronte Barratt"] ", the London bronze medalist."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The race went according to form, with Ledecky winning her second individual gold medal (after the 400 free) in 1:53.73, with Sjoström second in a national record 1:54.08, and McKeon taking the bronze medal. Pellegrini placed fourth, while Barratt tied for fifth with China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/129661"} "Shen Duo"] ". Franklin, not the swimmer she had been in 2012, did not make the final after finishing last her in her semi."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126653"} "Katie Ledecky"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:55.01 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "1:54.81 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "1:53.73 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/112272"} "Sarah Sjöström"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1:56.11 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "1:54.65 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:54.08 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129061"} "Emma McKeon"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align